spec:
  grid: 13-16 rows x 15-17 cols
  colors: one fg color (always 1) on bg (always 8), exactly 2 colors total
  object:
    shape: L-shaped rectilinear region = union of a horizontal arm and a vertical arm sharing a corner
    h_arm: 11-14 wide x 3-5 tall
    v_arm: 3-6 wide x 4-10 tall (standalone part, excluding overlap with h_arm)
    arm_thicknesses_differ: true -- the two arms generally have different thicknesses [observed]
    body_thickness: 3-6 (solver metric = mode of all fg run lengths >= 2; equals min arm thickness)
    missing_corner: any of TL/TR/BL/BR (all four orientations observed)
    margin: >=1 on all sides between fg bbox and grid edge (typically 1-2)
  features:
    tabs: 0-4 one-pixel fg protrusions on boundary (1 fg 4-neighbor, ray_len >= 3, plus side support n8>=3 or ray crosses 2*thickness-1)
    notches: 0-4 one-pixel bg dents on boundary (3 fg 4-neighbors, not adjacent to a tab)
    total: 2-6 per input (tabs + notches >= 1 each direction contributes)
    placement: on outer edges of either arm; may share rows/columns; must project through the body to reach the opposite edge in bounds
  transform:
    rule: |
      Each tab creates a notch at the opposite edge of the same row/column span.
      Each notch creates a tab just outside the opposite edge of the same row/column span.
      Notches adjacent to a tab source are skipped (they belong to the tab's local boundary).
    output_grid: same size, same bg, complementary jigsaw features added on opposite edges

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Build a clean L-shape as union of two perpendicular rectangles (h_arm and v_arm) with random missing corner, random arm thicknesses (3-6 each), and random arm lengths (>= thickness+2 for each arm)
    - Place the L on a 13-16 x 15-17 grid with >= 1 cell margin on all sides
    - Choose 1-3 feature pairs; for each pair, pick a random row or column through the body and a random direction
    - For each pair, add both the tab and its complementary notch on opposite edges of that row/column (this is the output state)
    - Derive the input by undoing the transformation -- remove every output-side complementary feature (delete each added tab, restore each carved notch)
    - Validate that solver body_thickness computes correctly and all features meet the ray_len >= 3 and support/crossing criteria
```
